  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader on a topic, I want the \"…\" menu at the top right to offer first page, last page and \"go to page N\" (with typed input), next to Rechercher and Filtrer, as the legacy app does. Operator report after a device test, 2026-11-07. Milestone M4 (parity).\n\n### Verified\n- **Legacy** (`MessagesView.swift:4692-4725` @ 2440d79): the top-right `ToolbarItem(.topBarTrailing)` \"…\" menu holds Sondage (when there is a poll), then Rechercher, then, when `currentMaxPage > 1`, a divider and `pageChoiceMenuItems()`. That item group is page 1, \"Page…\" (typed input), the last pages, and the last post.\n- **SwiftHFR** (`dev-swift`):\n  - The top \"…\" menu (`TopicReaderView.swift` around 100-110, `ReaderSearchFlow.swift:23`) has only \"Rechercher dans le sujet\" and \"Filtrer les posts\".\n  - The page choices exist only in LOT-186's bottom \"N / M\" menu (`ReaderPageControls.swift:44-58`, `pageMenu`: Page 1, Page…, the last pages, Dernier post), and the \"Aller à la page\" prompt is at `TopicReaderView.swift:113`.\n  - LOT-186 moved the legacy \"…\" page menu to the bottom bar (divergence D1) but did not keep the top menu's copy. That is the gap.\n\n### Fix\n- Reuse LOT-186's page items in the top \"…\" menu: extract them from `ReaderPageControls.pageMenu` into one shared builder, so both menus stay identical.\n  - Show them under a divider when `maxPage > 1`, as legacy does.\n  - Items: \"Première page\", \"Dernière page\", \"Aller à la page…\" (the existing typed prompt), plus the last-pages and \"Dernier post\" items legacy also lists.\n- Keep the bottom \"N / M\" menu unchanged.\n- Labels in French, VoiceOver labels, disabled while a load runs (as the bottom menu).\n- Tests: the shared item list for maxPage = 1, 2 and 40 (none on one page; first/last/page… otherwise), checked against legacy `pageChoiceMenuFinalTargets`.\n- Update LOT-186's spec D1 note (the page items now appear in both menus) and the GAP row.\n\n### Coordination\n#566 (reader stall fix) also edits `TopicReaderView.swift`, in other regions. Merge `dev-swift` before review.\n\n### Routing\nSonnet 5.5 writes, Opus 5.5 reviews. Claimed for the cloud child `ext/francoisgn-ui-581`.",
